{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"dc44f63e26c2a3d4","type":"group","x":-1515,"y":5673,"width":6115,"height":2117,"label":"40 Camping"},
		{"id":"98b6e42d6d88bf95","type":"group","x":-1552,"y":1271,"width":4952,"height":1409,"label":"Lagistics"},
		{"id":"fa48381217b041b7","type":"group","x":-1598,"y":-120,"width":3632,"height":1138,"label":"Belonging?"},
		{"id":"c17d7265fc5017b3","type":"group","x":-1552,"y":3040,"width":5312,"height":2080,"label":"30 Visit Anne"},
		{"id":"9e5d9db90ec3b1fd","type":"group","x":-5064,"y":-2353,"width":3004,"height":2193,"label":"Inbox"},
		{"id":"07ac2475860993d0","type":"group","x":-1593,"y":-1319,"width":3173,"height":959,"label":"From Then To"},
		{"id":"ba0dc42140919e15","type":"text","text":"there's like a special fund that was set aside for Savanna's return. Emma could basically mention it and be like yeah we'll probably have to pull some of Ben's half of Savanna's money, Jane will need it to buy a house for her and Ben live in. Like it could be framed from that angle of like there's a portion of the money that belongs to these two because it was set aside for Savanna, because Sara wanted to have three sources to welcome Savanna back in with open arms. I think that would really fit Sara, to have made that sort of financial decision a long time ago. Since like I said they have money to burn.","x":800,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0799c1affea20558","type":"text","text":"Does Anne know about Emma phasing to a ghost sometimes? Maybe it started after strangerville? Like Emma was staying on the third floor of the house, and one day or night she was napping or sleeping, and Anne was just like walking down the hall or into the living room, and found a ghost form Emma like haning from the ceiling by her foot or something like that. \n\nAnd so Anne was like \"Emma!\" No response. \"Emma wake up sweeite!\"\n\nAnd Emma like woke up, slipped fully out of the high ceiling, and phased back to being solid, so Anne caught her. ","x":20,"y":5200,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a9c750ff5756cf13","type":"text","text":"Jane is going to need a large sum of money, where does Sara want that money to come out of? That sort of thing. Sara is sort of the one in charge, but not with the like rule with an iron fist sort of way, these are her daughters. They choose to let her lead, they intentionally follow. This is genuine care, not threat of excommunicado. Anne isn't afraid she'll be punished if she doesn't get Sara's approval, Anne genuinely wants Sara's input.","x":1080,"y":4560,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"08153366a60d6fc8","type":"text","text":"This will really show Grant the world that he has stepped into. Because Sara and them aren't living in the woods because it's cheap. They're doing it because it fits Cass's needs, no one in his family stresses about money. ","x":-960,"y":4600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e4e712553a5ae2a4","type":"text","text":"I guess it is a sort of grief? It's a feeling that's hard to label for me, just this idea that he has been struggling so much for so long and there was no need for any of it. He never needed to work at all, Savanna could have come back to the family and would have been handed a house outright owned, no mortgage no rent nothing. Savanna might not have directly known that, but she never even got in contact with them, she never asked for help. She pushed them away, she attacked Emma in front of everyone. Like Jane and Sara and Anne were all there to watch. And still there was a fund for her, there was money set aside in case she ever changed her mind, well I guess from Sara's perspective more of when she changed her mind but well you know. I don't know I guess it just to me it just fits with the reaction that Sara had when she found out that Savanna was gone gone. This wasn't just a hope or a daydream, Sara assumed it was going to happen and did the necessary adult preparations, just the normal stuff that you do. This was real to Sara, she didn't know it was never going to happen.","x":1240,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c3859eecb3705bb2","type":"text","text":"I'm not seeing this as Grant being impressed with wealth or something like that, more just Grant's head is completely boggled because the concept of financial insecurity has just utterly been erased from his existence for the rest of his life. It just makes his past seems so meaningless. He has spent so much time stressing out about how to get Ben new shoes for school, when all along his extended family had a nest egg tucked away that can just casually buy a house for Ben to live in. And I mean technically it could buy a house for Grant too, but they don't make decisions the way Grant is used to making financial decisions. They make people decisions and support them with money they don't make money decisions and then try to make people work around them. Grant is used to having to fit him in Ben around the limits of money. This shows him that that entire concept just got flipped on its fucking head so hard.","x":1680,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"319c732da5b59490","type":"text","text":"I just sort of had this little like moment in my head of like it's just Emma and grant, and grants like um what fund were y'all talking about earlier. And Emma is like well yeah of course Sara set aside a fund for Savanna, she figured if she came back she'd probably need like a house or something, so she had money set aside. Sometimes it wasn't that much money, we had to dip into it a bit when everyone split up, I guess that could have been when you were like a baby, but Sara made sure it got refilled afterwards. That's where she put almost all of the money from those fat paychecks she got while she was in the military back in Strangerville. Though, we've all put some money into the fund, and the family's savings in general. ","x":2120,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"97ddc783d9a05922","type":"text","text":"Because like I'm picturing how Grant would feel about that, just this idea that Sara was throwing her paychecks into a fund that is now for him when she didn't even know he existed. Like he would recognize that that's someone working to take care of him, similar to that the popcorn recipe with Jane we're just like oh well Jane was always there, Sara was always there it was just completely invisible because it was a savings fund that he knew nothing about.\n\nBecause knowing a lot of it came from when Sara was in the military might make him feel like it's Sara's money, but Sara insisted the Savanna Fund be split in half and that one of those halves is Grant's. Like I said maybe they have to dip into Grant's half a little bit to get a house for Ben, but Grant won't care about that. Especially in the state he's in right now, he'd probably give the whole thing if Ben needed it. \n\nI'm also thinking that at first this might scare grant. He's used to the other shoe drops, he's used to favors come with strings. He thinks he doesn't understand Sarah and it scares him. But the thing is he actually understands her better than he knows. Because he's been doing the same exact thing for Ben, being there just because he's family. He didn't actually have to take care of the kid. He didn't technically have to be the adult in the situation. But in Grant's mind there was no other choice on the table. Which is very similar to how Sara sees thing in such situations. \"Because you're on my crew, why are we still talking about this?\" type of mindset. Something like \"well duh, you're family.\" give or take. \n\nThough I don't think Grant will figure this out on his own, I'm not sure. Idk. Like he is clever. \n\nWell here, how about instead of Emma bluntly spelling it out, she just has an \"well of course, you're family.\" and that causes Grant to realize how Ben is family to him and therefore understand. ","x":2560,"y":4120,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"838043ba1cb9f1e3","type":"text","text":"I wouldn't say it's about trust for Grant. Just he has to struggle so much for such little money. It's like mentally he has a money need bar, and it being low is a huge source of stress for him. The idea of him needing to come to someone every time he wants to make a small purchase would feel like a threat. It would be a source of hypervigilance for his brain. Being just handed a debit card with more money than he's even thought about before solves that \"money need\" so much that it's staggering for him. Because the way I'm seeing this, Grant will have a hard time believing he doesn't need to struggle for money. So having reality hand him a huge \"Nope\" will help him get past that old mindset. Them just handing him more money than he's dreamed of having at one time before goes a long way to getting rid of that belief. Because I was trying to write some scene where Grant is like \"but that fund is Sara's money\" and it just wasn't working. And then I just had this light bulb moment that he'll be a lot less worried about money if he just has some money of his own. Knowing he just has money that he has full agency over will help him feel safe about money, which will help lead to him process things around that (because feeling safe = trauma comes out for processing), and because he is used to money is the limit of his reality. What's for dinner had NOTHING to do with what he wanted to each and EVERYTHING to do with how many shifts he's worked, what Ben has needed recently, and what BS Savanna has done recently. Like a box he can't see he's inside because he's so used to operating inside of it. And Anne just casually shatters the illusion of that box. More money for Grant is more possibilities, because the edge of possibilities has been money for him for so long. And this naturally helps his curiosity, because just like seeing Emma going noncorporeal caused him to go \"cool, so solid is optional, how does that work?\" having this money just dropped on his head will cause him to go \"so being limited by money is optional, what are the real limits?\" it just might take a bit longer. Well and cause him to look at what he wants, because before what he wanted was outside the limits of his limited by money reality. That reality just expanded to include a LOT of his wants. \"I can't do that for myself, I don't have the money\" just got thrown out the window for a lot of things. Now he can afford to buy himself a fancy coffee or new shoes or festival food or a snow board from a vending machine or whatever. Like I said, for him it's not about permission. Agency is part of it, but it's more about possiblity than permission.","x":4160,"y":4180,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d22a2d32b74c7286","type":"text","text":"\"I'll start the paperwork to get your own account setup soon. It'll take a few days for me to get the cards from the bank.\" Anne pulled out a debit card with her name on it and handed it to Grant, \"In the mean time use this one for anything you need. I think balance is around $10k or so? Doesn't really matter, it has overdraft protection of course.\" \n\nAnd then the conversation just moves on, leaving Grant with some emotional whiplash from how casually someone just dropped thousands of dollars into his hands. He can read the room and tell the conversation has moved on, he can tell they don't expect him to question it, so he doesn't. He just puts it in his wallet for now. ","x":4160,"y":3684,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fd0a95831cd42344","type":"text","text":"Because Emma's younger sister and lives in a Ravenwood Manor, the big one in the southern part of the map that like by default isn't inhabited. In my story she fixed it up and turned it into the proper elite mansion befitting a socialite. ","x":-880,"y":3960,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c008545dd8b460ba","type":"text","text":"Well yes of course they're not going to be all hushed tones about him or around him about the money. He's one of them. There is no question about rather he's part of the family. He's a teenager he's old enough to hear these things.","x":3200,"y":3640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"959526567d2941ba","type":"text","text":"Be careful with what Grant notices about Anne. Not the fangs or the glowing red eyes. But her mannerisms, tone, bodily language. Show that he doesn't go off of things like eye color but off of things like facial expression and body language. \n\nIf anything worries Grant in front of Anne, it's that he doesn't know the social rules for high class society. Though Anne is the good hostess, she'll also be reading him and putting effort into making her guest comfortable. ","x":-2040,"y":3520,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d801f0b5a1e54c85","type":"text","text":"he's a teen, maybe Anne just automatically assumes he wants a bank card in his name, so that he can you know spend money for little stuff (clothes, vending machines, ordering pizza, stuff that's rounding errors for Anne). But it'll take some time to get one with his name so she just tosses him one of the cards with her name to use in the mean time. Like not just he's told there's money for a house, but they just straight up hand him some money. Because this gives him agency, this gives him decision making power. And this agency helps with his natural curiosity going towards trying to figure out what he wants to do with his life. ","x":4160,"y":3160,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ca9abb38154318e7","type":"text","text":"Once they're in the Ravenwood Manor, Anne Emma Grant Kaylee sit together in you know some sort of room sitting on couches something like that. Probably having like tea or whatever. Ever the hostess, Anne provides drinks for her guests. \n\n\n\nAnd kind of like a side note Emma mentioned oh yeah Jane will be by later today she needs to buy a house so she'll need money, and Anne's like do you know how much so I can get the paperwork ready, and Emma's like well I'm really not sure she's out looking for a place right now, she wants to see what Ben wants to do see what's best for the kid, maybe a hundred thousand or two I don't think she's going to go for that big of a place. And like at least internally Grant's jaw drops through the floor. This woman is casually talking about $100,000. Probably one of those things were in the moment Grant is simply observing, but I think that's a thing that like he's not going to be able to be quiet about when it's just him and Emma alone again. And maybe Emma is basically like well yeah whenever you look to buy a house just come talk to and she'll make the numbers work and we'll get you something, probably when you're older though. I mean I guess if you really want your own house as a teenager we can talk about it, but like I'm not sure living alone is the best thing for you right now. And Grant might basically be like I can just walk in there and ask her for that kind of money, and Emma's like well yeah you're part of the family duh. You're a Yootz hun.","x":920,"y":3160,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"50faa898f27b48e9","type":"text","text":"fat checks when they were in the military","x":2240,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"5030d883513b6f34","type":"text","text":"And so it's just like another complete paradigm shatter for Grant just this idea that like suddenly money is never a problem for him ever again. Like he's going to quickly understand the financial reality that yeah sure some members of the family have income, but because they choose to. We all work together we all help each other, and some of us sometimes don't have income and that's fine. Sara and Don certainly aren't working right now, and Emma's only doing the grimturn thing because she wants to not because she needs the money.","x":920,"y":3640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"6860c236b0926579","type":"text","text":"\"Ah yes, that will take some paperwork.\" Anne tapped her nose thinking. \"I might pull a bit from a few of the other funds as well, I'll need to run the numbers.\" She dropped her hand and smiled at Emma. \"Thank you for the heads up dear sister, that way I can start that prep work now.\" ","x":220,"y":3920,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"759984aa35609027","type":"text","text":"And for Grant this is probably another one of those things that should be reassuring but like on some level scares his nervous system. Every element of his concept of reality is rapidly shifting, and this is just been like what like day two day three? I think day two. Like this is a rapid shift for him, but also gives him the confidence to quit that stupid job in the city.","x":1480,"y":3640,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"abc61368c49d5ed6","type":"text","text":"I feel like this \"crafty pair\" is refering to a certain memory? I mean, Emma did live in Anne's house for a time. So she's gotten to know her vampire nieces. ","x":-480,"y":3960,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b5fe16017e93a842","type":"text","text":"Oh and meeting Anne herself is going to be a bit of a at least mental note for Grant. Because Anne is a born vampire she doesn't have a dark form. Yeah Grant has pieced together that Sara and Don are vampires, but they both have dark forms that he hasn't seen. Meaning he hasn't seen their fangs. They don't have fangs on a normal daily basis, they only have things in dark form not in regular form, and he's only seen them in regular form. Anne cannot hide her fangs, she has no separate form. She has fangs and glowing red eyes at all times, it's a weird quirk of her wonderfully unique biology of being turned in utero. And Emma probably won't think to warn Grant about that, because again for her it's just Tuesday. Like that's just part of her sister along with her blood red hair that she inherited from Sara. It's not abnormal and of note for Emma. Sure Anne didn't get those fangs and glowing eyes until she was a teen, but Anne hit that millstone years before Grant was even born. It's been so long it isn't something Emma thinks about. And Anne is this bubbly social life it's going to be like \"Welcome, pleasure to meet you darling!\" Because Anne did not get Sarah's tough nature. Anne can be ruthless, but it's completely different from her mother. Her type of ruthless is social ruthless, the kind of shark that a socialite needs to be sometimes. She knows how to play the game, but she doesn't play it when it's just family. She's completely charming and nice and friendly and proper and again giggling in her ankle length formal dress. \n\nEmma introduced Grant to Anne & Kaylie, and explains that Grant is Savanna's. Emma also explain that Savanna is gone, and Anna will just be like \"oh my gosh I'm so sorry Em\" and hug her. \"You let me know you need anything sweetie.\" \n\n\"Thanks.\" Emma's smile was soft. \"For the moment, just the camping. I need a trip out to the Falls.\"\n\nAnne's smile was knowing as she nodded. \"Don't let that Grim Reaper make you return to work too early.\"\n\nIt's almost a juxtaposition, she's the least normal looking one on a daily basis, but like socially probably the most normal of the bunch? At least by human standards. And to Emma, she's just Anne. She's always been polite, proper, favored formal attire, and been kinda eccentric basically. ","x":-120,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a77379acc5650054","type":"text","text":"Emma could be like well we need to go pick up the camping gear from my young sister's house, her house is bigger so we store things there. And Grant is completely caught off guard by Emma's casual \"bigger\" when he sees it. \n\n\"Oh, and family context,\" Emma figured it was better for him to have some idea of what he was walking into, \"Anne is my younger sister. She lives with her partner, Kaylie, and their two daughter, Clara and Lorelei.\" \n\nSo he and Ben had cousins. Grant wondered how much more family hadn't he known about.\n\nAfter a short pause Emma added, \"You'll probably want to avoid being alone with the girls if you can.\" \n\nGreat waited but Emma didn't say anything else. \"Because they're girls?\" I mean yeah sure adults are often suspicious of teenagers of the opposite sex in the same room, but like why did it need to be said? \n\n\"Hu? Oh right.\" It was easy to forget that Grant didn't know these things. \"They got their things as toddlers. Their thirst for blood too. They're good kids, but they're a crafty pair.\" She chuckled. \"It doesn't help that they're about your age but still just children.\"\n\n\"I'm not a little kid.\" And he wasn't about to be treated like one. \n\n\"Well no you aren't, but they are. Vampires don't age like humans.\" Based on his expression, he wasn't getting it, so Emma just said, \"You'll see when we get there. Just don't underestimate them. They have at least part of their super strength and speed.\" ","x":-680,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2b60f792e2b50ef3","type":"text","text":"Emma will want to stop by her own house to pack a few things, so Grant is going to get his first taste of her haunted house. Maybe even his initial reaction is that it's interesting. ","x":-1240,"y":3360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"bd02fcb79bc83fe3","type":"text","text":"And maybe Jane also does something that is tiny to her, that accidently causes another huge shift for Grant: she asks \"What about you?\" and he's like \"hu?\" and she's like \"What about you? Found something you love yet or still exploring?\" And Grant just says \"still exploring\" not because he thinks he is but because he actually has no clue how to respond, he hadn't even considered the question. And Jane is just like \"enjoy the journey\" or \"good stuff\" or something like that. Meanwhile either then or at some quite moment alone later, Grant realizes he wasn't even looking. The idea of looking might scare him at first, but that awareness causes a shift. Because like, Grant never lost his curiosity, if anything his might be the strongest of the bunch, because of moments like how he was able to question Emma about her ghost form the day they met. But that could be a big part of what gets him to point that curiosity at himself, seeing Ben and Jane modeling living this way. I could see it help Grant be a bit more bold than small things like buying a book on baking.","x":840,"y":8800,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d99fc7ccf28f7c3d","type":"text","text":"I'm thinking that Grant isn't there when Ben sees the horse. At first Jane thinks Ben is in wonder over fairies. Because of his wonder over her and then his wonder about the fairy place. But then she comes to realize he's not awestruck by fairies, he's awestruck by the world because before his world was the apartment and school in the city. So she starts taking him everywhere. Ben wants to see everything, so Jane takes him to see everything. It's just natural for her, he's a kid who wants to see what's out there. Of course she's going to take him, how else can he find what makes him happy? And one of the things that especially catches his interest is horses. Jane said his card could buy little things, but not big things. So he asks Jane if a horse is a big thing or if he can just buy himself a horse. Because that's how kid brains work. They live in a regular sized house (that doesn't have space for a horse) and have no where to put a horse, but that doesn't even factor in for Ben, because it wouldn't for any kid. But Jane's response ignore how it would be impractical. She says it's a big thing because first Ben needs to learn how to take care of a horse and keep it happy. And to Ben, that makes sense. And maybe he feels a bit of sadness, and before he can figure out what's next, Jane is like let's go see if they have any lessons you can take. And there's big bright glowing smile. And then at some point Ben and Grant are together again, maybe they hang out once a week or something? And Ben is like \"I rode a horse!\" And Grant's brain just doesn't know how to react at first. \"A horse?\" and Ben is like \"Her name is Sally and she's a brown horse, she's really sweet.\" Because of course to Ben these are the important details that must be shared. And I'm picture Ben wants Grant to see him ride a horse, so one day Grant comes to watch Ben ride, or watch Ben take his riding lesson. And that's when \"the money doesn't matter\" really sinks in for Grant. He sees Ben smiling, he sees Jane cheering him on and like maybe high fiving him or something. Not because anyone explains anything, but because of the feeling and emotions Grant gets from watching Ben do something simply because he wants to and it makes him happy. Grant doesn't KNOW money doesn't matter, he FEELS that money doesn't matter. And again this is going to help resolving his own trauma and stress responses and such. Maybe Grants tries to thank Jane, and to Jane it's nothing, or rather it was automatic? Or maybe Jane even misses what Grant is actually meaning and is just like I knew the fieldtrips were a good idea, I knew he'd find sometimes he loved, just didn't know what it would be. Because for Jane this was such an obvious thing to do that being thanked for it the way Grant means isn't part of her reality. It's a creative soul that supported her children mainly by selling paintings. Of course she's going to help Ben find his passion. To her anything else would be like depriving the kid of air: it doesn't occur to her.","x":320,"y":8800,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"cfde97c4a75cdeb3","type":"text","text":"When Grant is healing he's not becoming curious. He's recovering the freedom to use his curiosity for himself. It's a subtle but significant difference. ","x":2680,"y":8280,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"61ed0cc3b8b50074","type":"text","text":"Through all of their support, Grant is able to get to a place where he asks what do I want. And he finds out that I mean maybe he thinks this is a temporary want, but he wants knowledge. He wants learning. He wants to understand things he wants to find out things, he wants to understand the actual limits of reality. Like for example one day he'll be reading a book about vampire lore and he'll discover the recipe for the sunlight reversal cocktail, and maybe the book will discuss why it is luminescent and he will find this utterly fascinating. Not that he's ever going to drink one of those unless he decides he wants to be a vampire, maybe he tries on a few occult states, as experiments not as lifelong commitments. I could see him doing that deciding that like he wants to try being a vampire for a year or something. Not because he was ever going to be one for the rest of his life, but just because he's curious he wants to know. Because that's what he wants he wants to know he wants to learn he wants to understand he wants to find out. Which naturally turns into things like him wanting to go to university. His curious child turns into inquisitive scholar. He it might take him a while to figure out to really understand, but he likes learning things, that's the thing he loves he loves finding out stuff. He likes finding new information understanding new things. And not just because there's like a novelty factor, again he wants to understand the universe, that's his passion and I'm almost wondering if there's some way that he contributes to the family that has nothing to do with money. Probably not. But I guess maybe he could take up writing books, but I'm more picturing he discovers something or create something, no idea what yet. I do foresee him having several long conversations with Sara about the nature of the universe and her dark senses. I mean maybe he eventually learned something that he's deeply passionate about, but I just see him at least having a phase where the joy and the love is in the learning itself. He's not sure if he's exploring or if he's found what he loves, but he is loving exploring. ","x":2080,"y":8800,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d803e5a10e78c87f","type":"text","text":"Well because at first the curiosity comes \"back\" in a small contained way: he buys himself cheap books about how to do things. Because reading helps when his mind won't shut up. But this shift to exploring causes a more fundamental shift, and causes him to take steps to do things other than just buying cheap skill books. And yes Jane doesn't follow up, she trusts the process. He's exploring, she doesn't have to ask \"found it yet?\" she'll know when he finds it. Or she doesn't even think about it. Heck maybe she forgets the she asked because to her it wasn't a life-changing core memory, it was like asking about the weather. Because that's actually what Sara loves about her: Jane is passionate. Not just romantically. Passion is how Jane functions. She followed her passion of being a painter and a mother. Jane is sensitive sure, Jane isn't tough, but Jane has a big heart. Her passion is why she's so warm and fluffy when it comes to care. She's a wacky creative soul, always has been. She wore a witch hat to one of her first dates with Sara (and then asked Sara if it was too much, and was like no... well yes but I like it). Honestly that probably where Anne gets her \"bubbliness\" from, just Anne is the proper \"socially acceptable\" version while Jane is the version that's not afraid to look like a complete dork. Anne shows up over dressed, Jane is more likely to show up with pigtails and braids done by a child or covered in paint or some other wacky thing. She is enthusiastic and passionate and creative and artistic. She doesn't literally have the goofball trait, but she is a type of goof.","x":1460,"y":8800,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"998794f3a0f968b1","type":"text","text":"I think it's going to be interesting working through all this stuff with Grant and having him occasionally visit Ben, and so then he's observing how he's reacting to being around Ben again. In small doses & visits. I'm picturing like Grant suddenly understood how Jane could so easily just smile at Ben like that, because it becomes easier for Grant. He doesn't phrase it this way but he starts reaching a point where he has the space to be authentic with Ben, the smiles start being more real and less forced. So their relationship starts to shift into a place that's healthy for Grant, as it becomes not just all about Ben. And as Ben grows and goes through the natural stages of development, I could see Ben just automatically be more curious about what's going on with you Grant? Not because he's becoming as massively curious as Grant, just because I'm not sure how to phrase it. Sure Grant was really sensitive to how Ben felt, and was really trying to respond to his feelings, but that doesn't mean Ben didn't do the same thing in a different way. Grant did more of hiding feelings Ben was more honest with his feelings, but Ben would have also been sensitive to how Grant felt. And maybe on some subconscious level or something like that, Ben wasn't asking Grant how Grant was doing because some part of been understood that wasn't on the table, Ben tried to talk about happy things in a child way of trying to cheer up Grant. Like like Ben wouldn't even be aware that he was doing it. It would be purely a subconscious kind of thing. Kind of like that same part of Ben that could tell Jane was safe automatically starts to be able to tell that Grant has the mental bandwidth to talk about himself, and again this is just something been senses automatically he doesn't even know he's doing it.","x":-1209,"y":8217,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"25680bacabe7b110","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Long Term - authentic with Ben.md","x":3500,"y":8417,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"8b87fd5416d910a0","type":"text","text":"Well and it removes some of the \"needing provide\" burden from Grant. Before if Ben wanted hot cocoa, Grant had to figure out how to make it happen (and if it were possible to make it happen). Now Ben just buys the hot cocoa. Grant doesn't need to do anything. He doesn't even need to be there. It's one less thing that needs stress and attention from him. And it means Ben can have things he's wanted, things any kid would want, like hot cocoa at a winter festival, and Grant can just watch him enjoy it or look at the selfie's Ben took of him enjoying it or listen to the story or whatever. Where as before that wasn't critical for survival and therefore outside the realm of possibility, they wouldn't have even gone to a winter festival in the first place. I think Ben will adapt to this very quickly. Because he never had as much stress attached to it. To some degree he didn't ask Grant for such things, but not out of fear. Because even when Grant kindly explained he was sorry that they couldn't, even if Grant was smiling, so part of Ben would have understood that Grant was sad that the answer was no. Grant would have masked the stress, but Ben would have been able to tell it at least made Grant unhappy on some level. Ben didn't learn to be scared to ask for things, just he may have stopped asking for things because those things just weren't options for them. But then Ben gets a card and I think he'll quickly learn that now when he wants something generally the answer is yes. Maybe at first he's asking Jane if he can buy every little thing with the card, and Jane her warm fashion explains he doesn't need to ask. Maybe she tells him if it's too much money, it just won't work (kid wording of \"transaction limits\") and assures him he won't get in trouble, even if he loses the card, he should just tell them so they can fix it. Like I said I think Ben will adapt to these changes without the massive trauma issues that Grant is having. And if Grant notices that, I think his response would be like \"good, I'm glad Ben doesn't have to deal with this\" Grant doesn't mind being the one that has to deal with all the fallout of the stress & trauma and such. In some ways, Grant might see that as \"mission successful\" because he protected Ben. The key part of that phase being past tense. He did what he could for Ben, and now the fight is over. Like how Sara doesn't mind that she had to drink blood for Anne. Well that and a lot of trauma survivors talk about finding purpose in their suffering. Grant's suffering had clear direct literal purpose, so that will help him accept & process that trauma. Sure at first the nightmares are horrible, but once he realizes all this, the nightmares themselves don't have to change, his opinion of them will: \"good, that's another nightmare Ben doesn't have to have.\" Like he'll still be moving towards healing, he'll still want the nightmares to go away, he'll still see it as a good thing when they do start to fade & go away, but while he's still dealing with the symptoms, it will help him reframe it. Like the Buddhist thing that says pain is unavoidable but suffering is optional. Meaning you can't avoid stubbing your toe & the pain from it, but you don't have to let it break you. You can observes the pain instead of freaking out about it. Grant will naturally drift towards that sort of mindset. Like I said the same mindset Sara has about her stomach, a mindset rooted in acceptance of how things are, bad parts included. That yes waking up in a cold sweet from a night terror is uncomfortable, but he's come to see how it's like how having a cast is annoying: it's part of the healing process. So I guess I'm saying Grant will come to accept the healing process, and how at times it's uncomfortable, but that won't upset him. He'll be less confused about it. While Ben won't have any of this. Again Ben didn't have all this stress, so adapting to this massive change won't take as much for him. And maybe to some degree that is a sort of inspiration to Grant? Maybe Jane suggest they go to like a winter festival, and Ben is just happy. He does things like buy himself hot cocoa and it helps Gratn realize he deserves things like buying himself hot cocoa. He realizes he deserves wants too.","x":-160,"y":8800,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c07859735e4d4aec","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/40_CabinTour.md","x":-1440,"y":5820,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"1e2a719240683087","type":"text","text":"Sara might look at them six months later and think, \"There it is: Balance.\"\n\nGrant and Emma would probably never use that word.","x":-1320,"y":9000,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0221952721fd55b8","type":"text","text":"If Grant ever finds out that is was death that sent Emma, I'm picturing like a thankfulness to the universe, or at least death. This would certainly make death something Grant doesn't fear. \n\nBut I almost wonder if it would make Grant do something like get the same job as Emma so he can talk to Grim. Not that Grim will tell him anything? Or at least not much. \n\n\"There are things that are not for mortal minds to know.\" \n\nGrant paused, \"So are there minds that aren't mortal?\" He held up his pencil to point at the reaper. \"Like yours for example?\" \n\nGrim made a noise Grant couldn't make sense of, and looked to Emma. \n\n\"That's his laugh.\" \n\n\"Hu.\" Grant added 'can laugh' to his notes. ","x":-120,"y":9760,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"7021b396640a01d6","type":"text","text":"Maybe Emma basically has this routine of phasing to her ghost form at least once a day? Before bed. Grant would start to notice. \n\nOr maybe every morning and evening? Not sure. \n\nMaybe there's some point during the day when they're out that she feels the need to phase? And Grant notices her rubbing her hands and therefore is like here, hide in here so you can phase. ","x":5580,"y":6700,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2eb687fd853913a3","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Grant asks to stay with Emma.md","x":4120,"y":6807,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e4aa23cfcfc31ddd","type":"text","text":"Maybe there's a scene later when he's staying at the Falls (or later when he's at Emma's house?) where it's late at night and he's just looking at the debit card. Either the one in Anne's name or if he has his card where he's just laying in bed looking at the card, and just doesn't believe what he's seeing on some level. \n\nMaybe there's a moment where he thinks to himself that he can't afford something, but then when he's looking in his wallet, he sees the card from Anne, and remembers that yes actually he can. \n\nMaybe Emma mentions he'll want some bug spray from the ranger station before they go hiking. \n\n\"Bugs don't really seem interested in me anymore, not since I started phasing.\" Or she has some leftover from last time or something? Idk. Oh yeah because she goes hiking while he sleeps on the couch. \n\nMaybe Emma can tell he's hesitant, but don't step in to do it for him. She knows Grant was taking care of Ben, and therefore that he knows enough to handle buying stuff by himself. She knows he's not helpless. \n\nThis kinda forces him into using the money from Anne, well, assuming he doesn't use the money from his job? I don't know if he would have a joint account with Savanna, or if he would just have cash? If he's a server, then just cash. Which would also mean Savanna couldn't touch it. He could do things to hide it from her. Or maybe have some special account.\n\nOr maybe he sees how much the bug spray costs, and it's like ouch, but then when he opens his wallet, he sees the card from Anne and uses it, or at least he thinks about.\n\nANyway, while he's there, he could notice the herbalism books for sale, and maybe wonders about them. Doesn't buy them but he could not be sure if he saw those on the bookcase back in the cabin. ","x":5080,"y":6740,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"38fc78284ae07317","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/05_Reaping.md","x":-1400,"y":-1080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"8c07e0752e074bc0","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Camping Summary.md","x":4800,"y":6000,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"119faea887215445","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Grant Summary.md","x":4960,"y":5400,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"92583d85f173e16a","type":"text","text":"To be clear, back in the apartment he did feel hunger and he did eat, but like a typical trauma survivor, he's not in touch with his body. So as he heals, he's going to get more in touch with his body, which from his POV is going to be like turning up the volume of those signals. \n\nAnd by running on empty, I don't mean literally never eating, but I'm speaking emotionally. He doesn't have anyone emotionally supporting him in the apartment. Anyone who's there for him. Anyone he can turn to for help. Anyone who can take over when he's having a bad day or is sick. If him and Ben get a stomach bug, no one else is going to clean up the mess. I mean maybe Savanna would, but that meant risking her anger. Savanna had the same hot headed nature Sara has, but without any Sara's management (like exercise & mindfulness) or the support Sara has in place to help her (Don, Jane, etc). \n\nBasically there were times where he was tired or hungry and his body wanted to stop, rest, and/or eat, but he had to push through and do those things later after doing something (school, work, cooking, etc) for Ben. ","x":5640,"y":5400,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c2935e382eb2f523","type":"text","text":"Ok so Savanna and Mckinley both have/had the purple eyes. So Grant isn't the only person he knows with them, but his relatives are the only people he's seen with those eyes. \n\nMaybe he doesn't remember his mom, but he's seen like a picture of her. And knows she had them. \n\nStill, they signal family to him, because they aren't common among like people in general. \n\nOr maybe not say \"only people\" but like call them rare? Still the point is that this signals genetic relatives to him. ","x":-700,"y":-1920,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"61d9bfd67ace531a","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/09_Arriving.md","x":-780,"y":-1080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e2b3c863f69d5317","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/13_RestMyEyes.md","x":-280,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fc057a28091f7704","type":"text","text":"Actually maybe the landlord would take in Grant, but only Grant. And maybe use Mckinley, because really Grant doesn't remember her much, so she's not \"mom\"\n\nGrant probably doesn't think of Savanna as a competent mother, but probably calls her mom especially around Ben just to make things simple. Savanna was the one \"raising\" him even before Mckinley died anyway. Savanna tried to give her daughter the chance to be a teenager, and then her daughter died. ","x":-840,"y":560,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"2609814ab9bf9bc7","type":"text","text":"maybe Sara's mannerisms when she storms off remind Grant of Savanna (I mean they were mother & daughter) but then the way Sara leaves instead of blowing up at everyone is a jarring anomaly to Grant. A welcome one, but a wait what do you mean she just left instead of taking it out on me & Ben? And then Jane explains. He might not fully get it at that point. But at the very very least it would quickly establish Sara as not like Savanna.","x":-280,"y":-1420,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"7d2e07f282ff2cc0","type":"text","text":"I'm trying to imply that Sara's bandage is from a wound from Cass's wolf. But not having the characters say it out loud because Cass has feelings like shame about it. Sara doesn't mind getting wounds from helping Cass, but Cass is still struggling with it. For Cass it's upsetting to come back to human form and see Sara (and Don) with new wounds. Sara knows it's upsetting for Cass, so Sara avoids talking about it in front of Emma and these new people that are with her (Grant & Ben). \n\nMaybe after becoming a vampire Sara doesn't often use the wraps, because with dialing back her vampire strength and her vampire healing, she doesn't need them. But she's wearing them here with Cass to compensate for having problems with adjusting her vampire strength and needing to not have down time (vampire healing is faster than human, but still takes some time and Cass's wolf isn't going to wait). ","x":-300,"y":-760,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"47107e9c53ce3ac7","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/12_FamilyTree.md","x":-840,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c945bef325d58f5b","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/11_Cooking.md","x":-1380,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"bf14bcae3b60a7e7","type":"text","text":"Jane knew what that growl meant without Cass needing to say it: her inner wolf was hungry. But Jane also knew Cass was still learning to listen to what she needed, learning to voice those needs wasn't the priority yet. So Jane didn't draw attention to it. ","x":-1380,"y":480,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d7ab895a5dfff3af","type":"text","text":"Maybe part of why Sara has to storm off is because of what she did in Strangerville, she's lost some of that mind-body connection, so it's not just her strength she's having some issues with regulating, it's her emotions too. So to some degree until she can build back up that mindful baseline, she can't use things like deep breathing. She's kinda stuck with her oldest methods: hitting as hard as she can.\n\nPlus like she literally just found out one of her daughters is dead and gone and she can't do anything about it. \n\nI mean maybe she was starting to get a handle on it (and some of the more mindfulness based stuff she learned during her first pregnancy is coming back and she's getting some ability to regulate her strength and emotions), but then she gets hit with just a massive wave of emotion over Savanna and she can't handle it for a moment and she doesn't judge herself for that. \n\nThis is one of the few times she loses her shit in her entire life, so I think she gets a pass. I mean she also went nuts in Strangerville, but she was alone and saving Don required going nuts. ","x":200,"y":-1900,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"dc048085db03468b","type":"text","text":"- [ ] You're going to fit in just fine with the rest of us. \n\nDon't make what Emma says imply Grant & Ben aren't part of the family or are joining the family. They've been part of the family since they were born. ","x":-100,"y":560,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"928e44cc5dee642b","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/14_JaneWasAlwaysHelping.md","x":320,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"71f397331cd65956","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/15_Sara.md","x":800,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"363a0aa692ce7e89","type":"text","text":"It takes things like sparring with another vampire, going up against someone else who has that superhuman strength and speed. Or at least a fraction of it compared to her. That's why later Gibbi when she knows that Savanna is dead and gone, she turns to sparring with Don. Because she's not able to regulate that dial so much at the moment, she's kind of getting that ability back but death of one of her kids messes up that delicate restoring. She's lost her fine-tune calibration of that dial and it's just kind of turned up at all times, so she knows she can't regulate herself down to using a punch bag, she needs something more durable and buy something we mean her friend Don, because he's the second vampire she turned. Well okay I guess technically because he's a vampire, but whatever not the point.","x":800,"y":400,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0f5eeba6f7f230f4","type":"text","text":"And I guess to me this whole like infertility and choosing to be pregnant and all of that stays consistent even decades later, like that's a factor in why she's so torn up about one of her kids being dead and gone. That's why she wanted Savanna to come back but at the same time didn't force it. She gave her daughter choice. Free Will has always been a part of how she operates. And yet at the same time she holds each of her daughters dearly.\n\nthe infertility is a factor how much she loves and values for daughters because she never expected to have them, she doesn't take them for granted.","x":800,"y":800,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"90bb1aa5807f25fd","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/22.2_MorningPancakes.md","x":320,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f0bb441e97b415a5","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/20_BenAsleep.md","x":-1240,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d53dab695d9d3097","type":"text","text":"Grant initially looks for Ben, and Jane has tucked Ben in for a nap because his little system needs a break. \n\nMaybe they get outside.\n\nIdk, I might prefer the \"where's Ben?\" \"Oh I already laid him down to sleep in my tent over there\" type of sequence.","x":-1240,"y":2140,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"bf9231a5eb64df99","type":"text","text":"And he made living on the thirst floor of Anne's house really dangerous. ","x":-680,"y":2080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f53488f3e6eed555","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/25_Meal.md","x":2320,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"69ed22a06ea31e34","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/23_SleepingIn.md","x":820,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"15ffb32f23952a57","type":"text","text":"Okay so I just realized I have Jane and Ben there and then suddenly Jane and Ben have been gone for a while. Time space continuum whoopsie. Maybe it's just that Jane was in the cabin, and so Ben wandered off to the cabin to go tell her that Grant's awake and wanting food, and maybe she's already making like lunch or something? I don't know or maybe she was around the fire with Emma and ben, again not fire lit it's the middle of the day, but Ben heard Grant stirring, Ben came into the tent, grant talked about food, been totaled back out of the tent until Jane that Grant wanted food and so they've headed off to the cabin to cook something, and that's why like it's just Emma that's there when Grant comes out of the tent or like is finished using the bathroom or whatever, and Grant might ask where Ben is at, or just confirm that he's in the cabin or something. Or maybe he's too stressed out about the school in the laptops to think about that? Like it's actually his defenses coming down one by one, but they are coming but it's one by one so like the constantly track Ben's location has come down, but the make sure the school is informed has not. And Emma could say that like you know Jane was planning on taking Ben with her to look at places later today, and then in her head she's thinking because we didn't want you to wake up and him not be here because we figured you wouldn't like that. And most of the conversation still goes the same about talking about going camping in granite falls instead of gibbi point. ","x":1320,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"9aa332daabffa4ff","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/24_Laptop.md","x":1820,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c0b787dc76e22607","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/21_GoGhost.md","x":-680,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"ffe77a2f043871cc","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/22.1_MorningTea.md","x":-180,"y":1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fd8733f1e7fd0f09","type":"text","text":"\"Yeah, Anne's house is the biggest, so we store things like the camping there. And the family vault/museum.\"\n\nidk what they call the storage of all the collectables & such that they've found in the basement of Ravenwood. ","x":-3040,"y":-1600,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b418f269ea0c5e05","type":"text","text":"Ben will probably have mixed feelings about Grant not living with them. But maybe Jane explains it to him? \n\n## How?\n\nWell, and I guess Ben got used to older people telling him no in some way. Teachers say no. Grant would have to tell him things like \"sorry buddy we can't afford it\" and similar lines. Maybe at first Jane phrases it like Emma and Grant are taking a trip while we get moved into our new house, and promises that she and Ben can take a trip later. \n\nAnd maybe they stay away from \"Grant wants to live with Emma\" and stick more to like \"Grant is going to stay with Emma\" because it takes want out of the equation, which I feel is less open to why. Grant wants to live somewhere else kind of invites why doesn't Grant want to live here. Whereas well Grant is going to stay somewhere else, Ben might just fire away under one of those adults say no kind of things where he just goes with it. \n\nI mean he might ask if he's still going to see Grant, possibly with a big frown on his face, and Jane will be like of course sweetie oh come here and hug him and stuff. \n\nBecause I think I'm going to say that Sara Jane and Emma all just kind of know not to explain Grant's need to heal from the stress to Ben, and Grant will not want to explain it. Grant will just sort of inherently know that there's too much of a risk of Ben blaming himself, when none of it's Ben's fault and all of it is Savanna's. \n\nBut yeah I guess that does kind of make some inherent sense, if all the adults are like well this is the way it works now, Ben's more likely to just roll with it due to his age. I mean when he gets older he might start asking questions, but when he's a teenager or a young adult, not when he still a child. ","x":6820,"y":6660,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"9a3f9001210802bd","type":"text","text":"Grant might worry that Ben could be having nightmares too, but one quick call to Jane will let him know that nope, Ben is fine. He's excited about his new house, and has his own bedroom, and Jane says he can decorate it however he wants. ","x":6200,"y":6580,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"243f8cafecb047d6","type":"text","text":"With the popcorn, make sure Grant thinks about how it's about that Jane was helping them all along. It's not about \"oh Savanna didn't entirely reject everything\" it's about Grant knows he can trust Jane, because Jane is familiar, Jane isn't totally new. Without knowing it, a part of Jane has been there helping them all along. It's part of why Grant relaxes. He's not moving to something new, he's coming home to who he's always been. He might not have Sara's red hair, but he has her protective temperament. \n\nJane didn't know it, but she had help them get through some of the hardest times in that apartment. ","x":-4560,"y":-2080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0881e9c38023ed52","type":"text","text":"\"You let me sleep all day?\" Grant asked. \n\n\"Well, yeah. Sara said you needed it.\" Emma or Jane said. \n\n\"How would she know that?\" \n\n\"Hu?\" She turned to him. \"Oh right! Her vampire senses. Sara is deeply connected to the dark magic of the vampires. She just... knows things.\" \n\n----\n\nOk I'm not certain this is exactly how it's going to go, but I do want there to be some moment where someone is operating from something that's a given: if Sara senses it, then it's always true, and realizes Grant doesn't know that. They say \"Sara said...\" with the tone and attitude that it's a solid unquestionable fact, because they've all seen Sara's senses be right for... Anne's whole life (and Anne has a teenage daughter, Cass, by the time Grant enters the picture). But Grant doesn't see the connection of \"Sara felt it, there is must be true\" and questions it, and so they explain casually that Sara just knows things because of her vampire senses. \n\nWell I mean reading the vampire lore books might give him some idea of this, but it still might surprise him just how much they all trust her senses and how much she can feel. Because Sara and Anne aren't covered those books. They're not normal vampires. ","x":-4520,"y":-1200,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"9110c46b8d3581f2","type":"text","text":"Maybe Grant was the only person he knew with purple eyes, and that's part of why he notices them in Emma.\n\nAnd then he notices them in Jane. \n\nAgain building this trust, so he can let Jane worry about Ben and relax. ","x":-4120,"y":-2080,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"45d26e4781aae396","type":"text","text":"Emma tells Sara she'll take that crystal now. \n\nSara wants to feel if any Jane's crystals interact with Emma's ghost magic/form. \n\nOh, when Emma does phase into a ghost, what does Sara feel? Or does her protective mama bear nature override her senses? Sara is out of wack in a weird way. Probably need to look more into that? Like what affects it has. \n\nAnyway, this might kinda peak Grant's interest. Emma will have it near her at certain times. Sleeping, in the hot tub, etc when else. \n\nAnd once Grant is having nightmares (like not just the one) maybe Emma is like maybe we should both sleep near the crystal. \n\nThat will definitely peak Grant's interest. ","x":-3600,"y":-880,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c3e4375cea06b892","type":"text","text":"Like I'm kind of picturing this moment where Jane and Ben are somewhere and Jane notices been looking at something some little thing, and she's like you know what's up and he's like those look nice, and she's like do you want one, and he's like can we afford it because he's used to the way Grant phrased things, and she's like well of course. We can afford lots of things. Like no one needs to tell Ben that things are different now, things are just bluntly very different now. He doesn't live in a city he doesn't go to the same school he doesn't get told sorry we can't afford that, and his grandmother can fly.","x":7380,"y":6660,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"5d6872148d7b0ea4","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/41_FirstNight.md","x":-880,"y":5820,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b10414d86d635240","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Bedrooms.md","x":-1440,"y":6220,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"5a2b8967446c6b30","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Bookworm.md","x":-880,"y":6220,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d5f0175632342a33","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Couch nap.md","x":-300,"y":5820,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"9baa661593f02627","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Nightterror.md","x":260,"y":5820,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"e75587d1924432d8","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Tea for nightmares.md","x":260,"y":6220,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"1c2c76ffac0c6777","type":"text","text":"Mid week visit\n\nJane calls and says Ben is asking about a visit, and Emma is thinking about getting the crystals from Jane, and Grant is thinking seeing Ben, seeing the house he's living in now, might help with his fear about Ben's well being. \n\nSo they spend the afternoon at Jane's house. Emma can ask Jane for the crystals to help with sleep. Grant can as Jane how Ben is sleeping (just fine), and Grant can see things like the fully stocked fridge and Ben smiling and Ben happy about his bedroom, and so on. \n\nThen when they get back to the cabin, Grant just kinda quietly sits staring at the trees or something like that. He has so many things he feels at once. Seeing Ben safe is another \"oh it's safe enough to process trauma now\" type of thing. And things like Grant feels releaved that he has the cabin so he can just feel the stress and relief and do something besides smile for Ben's sake, and he's guilty about feeling that, and he can see he's too tired to keep up the fake smiles. Like he doesn't have it in him to keep them up around the clock and therefore likes that he has this private space to let the act down. Where he doesn't have to shove down everything he's feeling. Maybe he can kinda tell that those feelings aren't going to stay shoved down. He probably knew it was never healthy to do so, but before it was that or let Ben see them. I guess it's just another part of him learning to take care of himself, and more lived experience that helps lead to him building his framework. \n\nAnd Emma maybe makes tea, and maybe just quietly sits in the same room. Not to hover, just so he's not alone. \n\nI guess this will also feed into Grant's decision to stay with Emma, so that he still has that space for himself. Which is like a radical act of self care for him, but it takes a lot of the stress off him, so he has space to heal. Because Ben is ok, so he's allowed to heal. Because maybe he realizes he needs space, like how Cass does. Maybe he thinks about what Sara said, either now or later in the week. ","x":1560,"y":5820,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"4f93c805011c12a3","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Ghost Realization.md","x":1560,"y":6360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fb86d1a789ff9846","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Some Part Doesn't Know.md","x":2360,"y":6360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"7f7b4f3bddb183be","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Ghost Realization Notes Meaning.md","x":1960,"y":6360,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"b2477d91b064496a","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Popcorn at the Falls.md","x":2931,"y":5869,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"22894e5d9b0444d4","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/Activities.md","x":3640,"y":6020,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"fa01b21361472929","type":"text","text":"And yeah I think that does make sense that he would call his boss to ask for leave for his grandmother (adopted mother) dying, just because it's the \"old habits\" running.","x":-1440,"y":6760,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"a2c2d4bddea91ac7","type":"file","file":"Sims4-Yootz-Story/plans/spoilers/40_TheBoys/16_CabinMeal.md","x":1280,"y":0,"width":400,"height":400},
